```typescript
export type DispatchRecord = {
  id: number;
  operator: string;
  destination: string;
  priority: number;
};

export function selectDispatches(
  records: readonly DispatchRecord[],
  operator: string
): DispatchRecord[];
```

`selectDispatches` must return records whose `operator` exactly equals the supplied string, preserving input order. It must not trim text or perform case folding. Return an empty array when there are no matches or the input array is empty. The returned array and every returned record must be newly allocated, so mutating the result cannot affect the input. Do not mutate the input.

At runtime, throw `TypeError` if `records` is not an array, `operator` is not a string, or any record has a non-integer `id`, non-string `operator` or `destination`, or non-finite `priority`. Validate every record, including records that would not match.

